# benchmarks/.gitignore
#
# Enforces the AAP §0.8.2 / §0.6.2 constraints on the harness package:
#   - Binary profile artifacts (`*.cpuprofile`, `*.heapprofile`) MUST NOT be
#     committed — they are environment-specific (host CPU, kernel, Node.js
#     minor version) and may be very large.
#   - Timestamped result subdirectories under `results/` MUST NOT be
#     committed — every timestamped run produces its own subdirectory, and
#     only the `results/.gitkeep` sentinel that reserves the parent
#     directory is tracked.
#   - `node_modules/` MUST NOT be committed — `npm install` resolves the
#     harness's single declared devDependency (`autocannon`) from
#     `package-lock.json`, which IS committed (AAP §0.4.1 — "the implementing
#     agent will produce `benchmarks/package-lock.json` at execution time
#     and that lockfile becomes the authoritative version record").
#
# This file lives only inside `benchmarks/`. It does not affect the
# application package at the repository root — `[server.js]`,
# `[package.json]`, `[package-lock.json]`, and `[README.md]` are immutable
# per Constraint C-001 (`[README.md:L2]`, `[Section 2.6.2]`) and are not
# referenced from this file.

# Harness dependency tree — installed by `npm install` from package-lock.json
node_modules/

# Timestamped result directories — every harness invocation writes one.
# Match both forms produced by the scripts:
#   results/<unix-epoch-seconds>/  (e.g., results/1779303391/)
#   results/<utc-iso-basic>/       (e.g., results/20260520T190102Z/)
# The negation rules at the bottom preserve the .gitkeep sentinel that
# reserves the directory itself.
results/*

# Preserve the directory placeholder so the empty `results/` folder is
# tracked even when no run output exists.
!results/.gitkeep
